--8<-- [start:description]

If a channel holds a newer version of a requested package that can't be
installed, for example because one of its dependencies is only available from a
lower-priority channel under strict channel priority, the environment is updated
to the newest set that does solve and the command fails with the solver's
explanation, instead of reporting the environment as unchanged.

--8<-- [end:description]

--8<-- [start:example]

## Examples

```shell
pixi global update
pixi global update pixi-pack
pixi global update bat rattler-build
```

--8<-- [end:example]
